%% Bunny OS Phase 1 — Diagram 10 (file 15): Plugin Execution
%% Installation, permission declaration, invocation, sandboxing, revocation.
%% Core invariant: an extension NEVER receives ambient authority merely by
%% being installed (C16). Today's repo has signing but no isolation (§3.5).

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SH as Bunny Shell
    participant BR as Bunny Broker
    participant EM as Extension Manager
    participant POL as Policy Evaluator
    participant GL as Grant Ledger
    participant CREG as Capability Registry
    participant EC as Execution Controller
    participant SM as Sandbox Manager
    participant EXT as Extension Runtime
    participant AUD as Audit Service
    participant J as Durable Event Journal

    rect rgb(40, 48, 58)
    Note over U,AUD: INSTALL
    U->>SH: install extension X
    SH->>EM: install
    EM->>EM: verify Ed25519 signature over the file digest
    alt tampered
        EM--xSH: refused — never loaded regardless of policy
    end
    EM->>EM: resolve publisher identity and trust tier
    EM->>EM: parse permission manifest
    EM->>SH: consent surface in the action-class vocabulary
    Note over SH: "X declares: Read (this workspace),<br/>Send externally (api.example.com).<br/>Effective isolation and egress follow<br/>the constitution-resolved A4/A5 branch."
    U->>SH: confirm install and manifest receipt
    SH->>GL: record declared-but-ungranted manifest
    EM->>CREG: register tools, tagged with supplying extension
    EM->>AUD: install record — publisher, tier, signature status
    Note over EM,GL: NO grants are issued at install.<br/>Installation is not authorization.
    end

    rect rgb(40, 48, 58)
    Note over EC,AUD: INVOCATION
    EC->>CREG: resolve tool
    CREG-->>EC: tool + declaring extension + trust tier
    EC->>SM: prepare exact extension profile<br/>with no usable capability
    SM->>EXT: create isolated context
    EC->>POL: evaluateForAdmission(exact operation tuple,<br/>declaration, context and epochs)
    alt undeclared capability requested
        POL--xEC: deny — fails closed, no prompt offered
        EC->>AUD: undeclared capability attempt
        Note over POL: requesting outside the manifest is<br/>treated as evidence of compromise
    else declared but no exact active grant
        POL-->>EC: user-grant-required AdmissionEvaluation
        EC->>BR: surface exact request and stop this attempt
        BR->>GL: createRequest(ActionSpec, effect,<br/>extension subject and rendered digest)
        GL-->>BR: request id + expected version + digest
        BR->>SH: permission request projection
    else declared with matching active grant
        POL-->>EC: fresh user-grant-required AdmissionEvaluation
        EC->>GL: prepare matching reservation mutation
        GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>AUD: prepare AuditStart mutation
        AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>J: admitEffect batch<br/>(Grant + ExecutionStarted + AuditStart)
        J-->>EC: fsynced admission receipt
        EC->>SM: present receipt, exact ActionSpec and epochs
        SM->>SM: independently validate receipt,<br/>ActionSpec hash, extension epoch and grants
        SM->>EXT: materialize exact capability and invoke
        EXT-->>EC: observations
        EC->>EC: verify terminal outcome
        EC->>GL: prepare reservation terminal
        GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>AUD: prepare AuditTerminal mutation
        AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>J: finalizeEffect batch<br/>(Grant + Execution + Audit terminal)
        J-->>EC: atomic terminal receipt
        Note over EXT,EC: the result — including any tool<br/>description text — is UNTRUSTED INPUT<br/>and is a known injection carrier
    end
    end

    rect rgb(58, 34, 34)
    Note over U,AUD: REVOCATION
    U->>SH: revoke X
    SH->>EM: revoke
    EM->>GL: revoke all grants held by X
    EM->>SM: terminate running contexts
    EM->>CREG: deregister tools
    EM->>EM: cancel standing jobs created by X
    EM->>EM: mark memories created by X for deletion
    Note over EM: the extension epoch invalidates authority atomically.<br/>Context, registry, job and memory cleanup is<br/>an idempotent visible saga, not one transaction
    EM->>AUD: revocation record with what was removed
    end

    Note over EM,AUD: KILL SWITCH — a signed revocation list disables a known-malicious<br/>extension across all installs, with the user informed. Distribution must not<br/>create a phone-home requirement that violates local-first (§19.6).
